# Vendored known-good packages: the lock set.
#
# Arch Linux ARM rebuilds Arch's packages one at a time with no staging and
# keeps no dated archive, so when a library bumps its soname the repository
# cannot satisfy its own desktop for a few days and the old coherent versions
# are already gone from every mirror. This file, with the package files in the
# release named below, lets a fresh install drop in a set known to work instead
# of waiting for the build farm or compiling on the Pi.
#
# Regenerate both this list and the release from a machine where the desktop
# works, with install/arm/pin-packages.sh. Empty means the mechanism is dormant
# and install.sh falls back to building from Arch's recipe.
#
# release: https://github.com/jhirsh/omarchy-arm/releases/download/pinned-packages
#
# filename                                     sha256
